# Chapters forked from another project. `sh tex/import-check.sh` reads this file.
#
#   <file in this project> | <origin path> | <origin sha256> | <this file's sha256> | <date>
#
# Getting the two hashes:
#   shasum -a 256 "<origin path>"    -> column 3 (the origin as it was at the fork)
#   shasum -a 256 "tex/<file>"       -> column 4 (our file after adaptation)
#
# Column 3 disagreeing means THE ORIGIN moved. Read the diff and decide -- do
# not auto-merge. The origin is authoritative for the mathematics.
#
# Column 4 disagreeing means WE changed it. Write what was changed at the top of
# the file (`ADAPTED:` for notation, citations and references; `FIXED:` for a
# mathematical correction) and update this column. The checker cannot tell the
# two apart, so a human has to say which it was
# (CLAUDE.en.md, "Cross-project reuse").
